{
 "id": 98377,
 "name": "Mixed Reality Service Community Group",
 "is_closed": true,
 "creation-date": "2017-03-22",
 "description": "The Mixed Reality Service Community Group will work to define an open protocol that provides a mapping between geospatial or virtual coordinates and URIs.\r\n\r\nMixed Reality Service has numerous applications in areas as varied as gaming, autonomous vehicles, health &amp; safety, and affordances for the disabled. More details can be found at <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://mixedrealitysystem.org\">mixedrealitysystem.org</a>\r\n\r\nThis group will expand upon the work <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://hyperreal.org/~mpesce/www.html\">presented at WWW1</a>, and re-introduced in a <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-0Y548vLlxpIByOvIgaE2QcEPf_z_hKXs3Kj8wO5eh8/edit#slide=id.g1856b96749_1_8\">lightning talk</a> at the initial WebVR meeting in October 2016.",
